    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1607">

                <pb facs="1312" n="1196" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/93.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your
                    confidential despatch No. 19, of the 6th instant, in which you report a
                    conversation between yourself and Señor Obarrio, a member of the Panaman
                    Assembly, in regard to the proposed construction of the Panamá-David
                    Railway.</p>
                <p>A copy of your despatch has been forwarded to the Secretary of War.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—The President’s message to Congress
                        on departmental questions<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1607-f1"/> was read December
                        21, 1911; it refers to the Panama Canal and calls attention to the need for
                        legislation relating to the government of the Canal Zone, which should
                        approximate a military government.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
